# im an obsessive learner — for domain glyphs 📜

a **zoom-in** of `im_an.obsessive_learner` onto one lesson kind: the **glyph lesson**.

a glyph is a term on a surface with no room for a word. it obeys the term law — one concept, one symbol — and lands in `domain.glyphs/catalog.of=glyph._.md` + `catalog.of=glyph.axis=$axis.md`.

the failures, verbatim from the term rules: two glyphs for one concept · one glyph for two concepts · a glyph claimed with no record.

## ⚠️ .the repair cost is worse than a term's

a term appears in the contracts that use it. a glyph prefixes **every surface it marks** — a readme header, a stdout line, a status line, a declared config field, and every snapshot of all four.

⇒ a claimed glyph spreads at once, and **each surface makes the repair dearer**. catalog it in the round that claims it, or the next claimant greps, finds no match, and takes it.

## 🔴 .a grep proves a glyph UNUSED — never UNCLAIMED

a glyph may be **reserved** for a role that does not exist yet. it greps clean the whole time and is never free. **only the catalog settles it.**

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| you **claim** a glyph, on any axis | 🔴 catalog it. the row IS the claim |
| it is **not in the repo's palette** | add it to the palette first, with its one-line sense |
| a grep returns **no match** | that proves unused, never unclaimed. **read the catalog** |
| a grep hits **several surfaces** | one concept seen twice ✅ · a decoration that sorts no reader ✅ · two concepts 🔴 |
| you find a glyph in use with **no row** | 🔴 the arrears. add the row now |
| two copies of the record **disagree** | reconcile to the catalog; make the others its dependents |
| you coin a **third** glyph for a concept a marker covers | glyph-synonym drift. reuse the settled one |

⚠️ **check the code before you swap.** a type that names its own slots — a `mascot` field beside an `artifact` field — has already drawn the seam. a swap drafted against a misread of that seam moves hundreds of occurrences and repairs no defect.

## .the test — answer both, on the page, before the claim

> **1. does this glyph name what its subject DOES?**
> **2. what CONCEPT does it hold — and does another glyph already hold it?**

picked for looks fails 1. a concept already held fails 2, and the repair is **reuse**, never a coinage.

then update every published face that restates the catalog, so none drifts from the index.

## .see also

- `domain.glyphs/catalog.of=glyph._.md` — the index this obsession tends
- `domain.terms/term=glyph._.choice._.md` · `.reason.md` — the definition, the palette rule, the measured collisions
- `.for.domain.terms` · `.for.domain.invariants` — the peer kinds

> a grep finds what is used. only the catalog finds what is spoken for. 📜
